    "source_excerpt": "FDA label sections 11 (Description), 12.1 (Mechanism of Action), and 12.4 (Microbiology, Mechanism of Action): \"Each gram of NAFTIN ® Gel contains 20 mg of naftifine hydrochloride, a synthetic allylamine antifungal compound.\" \"12 CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY 12.1 Mechanism of Action NAFTIN ® Gel is a topical antifungal drug [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.4) ] .\" \"12.4 Microbiology Mechanism of Action Naftifine is an antifungal that belongs to the allylamine class.\" \"Although the exact mechanism of action against fungi is not known, naftifine hydrochloride appears to interfere with sterol biosynthesis by inhibiting the enzyme squalene 2, 3-epoxidase.\" -- Section 12.1 cross-references 12.4. The label calls the exact antifungal mechanism unknown, so mechanism_established is false; squalene 2,3-epoxidase inhibition is described as appearing to occur. Section 11 identifies naftifine hydrochloride as a synthetic allylamine antifungal compound, supporting small_molecule modality.",
